## 1. The workflow — build exactly this, in this order

The user journey, end to end:

```
Landing page (/)
  -> Sign up / Log in (/auth) — Google + email/password, local preview until Supabase Auth is connected
  -> EITHER: start the ONE free trial (7 days, no card) -> /dashboard
  -> OR: choose a plan (/pricing) -> paid checkout (Stripe, NOT live yet — see below) -> /dashboard
```

Rules:
- A user who is not logged in and tries to open /dashboard, /leaderboard, /concepts, /videos, /settings is redirected to /auth, then back to where they were going.
- A user who is logged in but has NO plan AND NO active trial and tries to open /dashboard is redirected to /pricing with the message "Pick a plan or start the free trial. You need a plan or the 7-day trial before the dashboard opens."
- Never send a logged-in user back to the landing page on login — send them to /dashboard. (There is no onboarding flow — the user goes straight to /dashboard after sign-up or trial start.)
- Logout returns the user to /.

### The free trial — THE rule that matters most. Get this right.

There is exactly ONE free trial. It is NOT per-plan. It is NOT "try Starter free for 7 days" or "try Growth free for 7 days".

- 7 days, no card required — no card is collected at all, nothing is charged automatically when it ends.
- Trial limits (show them wherever the trial is offered): **24h leaderboard only, follow 1 creator, 3 concept lists total, 2 x 10s videos at 480p (20 seconds total), watermarked.** No clones, no heroes, no 720p/1080p, no Instagram, no ad library, no coin packs.
- The trial starts ONLY from a trial CTA: the nav "Start free trial" button, the hero "Start 7-day free trial" button, the closing CTA button, and the trial banner on the pricing page. Every one of those links to `/auth/?trial=1`.
- After sign-up from a trial link, the trial starts immediately and the user goes straight to /dashboard. If the user is ALREADY signed in and clicks a trial link, the trial starts straight away (no second sign-in).
- Pricing cards do NOT have a trial button. Each card has exactly ONE button: "Choose Starter" / "Choose Growth" / "Choose Scale". Choosing a plan is the paid path. Since Stripe is not live yet (see Section 7), choosing a plan shows an honest notice: "Paid checkout isn't live yet. Stripe Price IDs for the plans aren't created, so subscribing can't take a payment right now. Start the 7-day free trial (no card) instead." — with a link to the trial. Do NOT record a plan choice as a trial. Do NOT start a trial when the user picks a plan.
- When the trial ends, generation locks until the user pays for a plan. Nothing is charged automatically.

### The recreate workflow — the two paths, in detail

When the user is on the dashboard and sees a viral video, they recreate it one of two ways:

- **Path A — Recreate here (in the app).** The user clicks "Recreate here" on the video card. They go to Concepts with that video pre-filled, and concepts generate straight away (no extra click). They pick a concept, tweak it or edit it, then go to the generator and make the video (Wan 3.0 default, up to 30 seconds, 9:16, native audio). They download it and post it on TikTok.
- **Path B — Recreate on Claude (themselves).** The user clicks "Copy Claude prompt" on the video card. A complete, ready-to-paste Claude prompt is copied to the clipboard and the button briefly reads "Copied ✓". The prompt contains: the viral video (format/product, creator, views, CTA, caption), the user's product and character (from Settings — if not set, it says so and asks Claude to suggest a character), and asks Claude for: (1) a concept adapted to their product, (2) a hook for the first 0–3 seconds, (3) a 5-shot breakdown with timestamps, (4) the caption and CTA word, (5) a video generation prompt to paste into a video tool (9:16, up to 30 seconds, native audio). The user pastes it into Claude, gets the workflow, and generates the video themselves. This is the same workflow the product's own users already use (Claude for concept/workflow, then a video tool).

