4. **The feed:** the viral videos as a grid of video cards, **4 videos in one line** on desktop (3 on medium screens, 2 on small, 1 on phones). Each card is the video itself, 9:16, filling the card. Data: `GET /api/v1/leaderboard?window=24h`. When the backend has live data, use it, ranked by velocity. When it returns demo data (Treg not connected), show the 14 real TikTok videos already on the site as the preview feed, ranked by their real view counts, with the honest banner **"Preview data. Real TikTok videos, ranked by views. Live velocity ranking connects when Treg is set up."** Never show a velocity number, caption, or CTA keyword that is not real — preview cards show only the real creator, the real views, and the real product.
5. **Hover-reveal (the clean look).** At rest the card shows only the video and a tiny bottom strip: **@creator** + views. On hover (desktop) the video plays (muted, loop) and an overlay fades in with: the product, the caption, views (and velocity in views/hour when the backend provides it), the CTA keyword as a small tag when there is one (e.g. 'Comment "WINGS"'), and the two recreate actions — **"Recreate here"** and **"Copy Claude prompt"** — plus a small **"Follow @creator"** text link underneath. On touch screens there is no hover, so tapping the card (not the buttons) toggles the same overlay and plays/pauses the video. Buttons under every card would add a row of chrome to each of the 4 cards and compete with the videos — the hover version keeps the grid pure video and shows actions only when the user is interested in that card.
6. **The two recreate paths (this is the product):**
   - **"Recreate here"** — goes to Concepts with this video pre-filled, and concepts generate straight away (no extra click). The user picks a concept, then generates the video (Wan 3.0 default, up to 30s, 9:16, native audio). This is the in-app video generation path.
   - **"Copy Claude prompt"** — copies a complete, ready-to-paste Claude prompt to the clipboard and briefly reads **"Copied ✓"**. The prompt contains: the viral video (format/product, creator, views, CTA, caption), the user's product and character (from Settings — if not set, it says so and asks Claude to suggest a character), and asks Claude for: (1) a concept adapted to their product, (2) a hook for the first 0–3 seconds, (3) a 5-shot breakdown with timestamps, (4) the caption and CTA word, (5) a video generation prompt to paste into a video tool (9:16, up to 30 seconds, native audio). This is the "generate it yourself on Claude" path — the same workflow the product's own users already use (Claude for concept/workflow, then a video tool).
7. **A small count line under the grid:** **"14 videos · 24h · preview snapshot"** (or "· live" when the data is live).
8. **Why it is laid out like this:** the user opens the app with one question — what went viral in the last day, and how do I make one like it? The sidebar and header make it feel like a real app, the stat cards give the at-a-glance summary a dashboard needs, and the feed is the product — the two recreate paths are one hover away. Nothing else competes with it.

### 5.2 Leaderboard — the full discovery browser
